        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>So, I've been considering what aspect(s) Adam and Christopher would be as singular entities.(ie, Wellspring is the aspect of progress, Wager Master is Chaos, etc...) due to comment on this&nbsp;episode.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHere's some ideas I had:<br />\r\n1) Adam is the aspect of sight(art), Christopher is the aspect of sound(speech). Doesn't quite work though, because they both do more than that, and speech in comics is written.<br />\r\n2) Adam and Christopher are twin entities of vision. Vision=art/how the world is seen and&nbsp;Vision=future/how the world sees itself. Again, not great, because Christopher is not associated with vision enough.<br />\r\n3) The obvious one; twin entities of story. pacing, tension, etc...<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAny other cool ideas?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAlso, i feel the question&nbsp;that the matriach asks is \"whether there was a world where she wasn't a villain/didn't kill all those people.\" then, in the story, she joins the freedom five because argent adept helps her before any very serious damage is done. This sets up for the long trip of guilt, repentance, and changing of names that the matriach goes through.&nbsp;</p>",
