      {
        "id": 264415,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-11-14T03:14:31.646Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I wish I knew what Justifier thought of this episode, but I don’t remember my former opinion, and I seemingly never posted anything about it.  Sadly, this is one of my least favorite concepts that C&amp;A have ever explored; I like almost none of the variations they went for.  The only interest I can see myself having in this reality is in a theoretical future Definitive OblivAeon, where Arcane Bunker or Parse-Omnitron might be a Mistgate character, like Windwalker or Cursor.</p>\n<p>There is one thing in this episode that’s great, but it isn’t the story premise, it’s in one of the letters.  They’ve mentioned before that they have universe numbers, but this is the first time they disclosed any of those.  Inversiverse is 999 they said; I wonder if Xtremeverse is 666.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-11-14T03:38:57.280Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
